WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:06.590
Fake X-Force scenes, a Chris Evans cameo,
underwater scenes with Vanessa, and not-safe-for-work

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:09.759
Disney jokes were all cut from Deadpool 2.

00:00:09.759 --> 00:00:13.389
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm explaining everything we never

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:18.210
got to see in the Deadpool sequel [plus details
on an extended cut of the movie.]

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.880
If this is your first time here, be sure to
subscribe to get all my Deadpool and Marvel

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:26.609
videos and leave a comment for a chance to
win some cool Deadpool 2 merch.

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:30.460
Spoilers ahead, of course, for the movie,
so take care if you've not seen it yet.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:35.320
It was fun meeting the new X-Force team in
Deadpool 2 even though our time with them

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.580
was pretty short.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.830
But if you'd watched the movie's trailers,
you probably thought we were going to get

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:45.500
more time with the new team than we did, including
action scenes with both Bedlam and Shatterstar.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.550
And that's exactly what the filmmakers wanted
you to think!

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:52.890
Yes, the movie's director and writers told
Uproxx that they filmed those extra scenes

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.860
with the actors in front of a green screen
knowing full well that they'd never put them

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:58.510
in the final film.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:02.280
It was all done with the aim of pranking the
audience, and at one point they were even

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:07.130
planning to make individual character posters
and standees of the X-Force members as well,

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:11.600
however, the Studio told them to hit the brakes
in case audiences got too annoyed when they

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.000
saw the film.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.950
The idea behind the marketing, of course,
was to make all those sudden X-Force deaths

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.220
more of a shock to viewers watching the movie
in the cinema.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:23.890
Which it certainly was though it was still
a bit of a shame to see so little of actors

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:26.740
like Terry Crews, Lewis Tan, and Bill Skarsgard.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:30.800
There wasn't any explanation in the movie
about where Cable got his mutant powers or

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.000
his metal arm from.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.160
However, there's a potential nod to his cybernetic
arm and the techno-organic virus from the

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:40.550
comics in a voiceover line in the trailer
that we never heard in the final film.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:44.590
In the film, Cable asks Weasel:
"What's the most pain you've ever felt?"

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:47.520
But this next line from Cable in the trailer
was cut from the movie.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.550
"Maybe the kind that leaves you more machine
than man."

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:55.930
Perhaps this audio was part of a deleted scene
or it could be an extended version of Cable's

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:58.580
monologue when he's interrogating Weasel.

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:02.560
And based on Cable's words, it sounds like
this would have added yet another Star Wars

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:07.680
easter egg to the movie, this time referencing
Obi Wan Kenobi's words about Darth Vader.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.259
"He's more machine now than man."

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:14.620
As for Cable's rich comic-book history, the
movie's writers told Vulture that they used

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:18.879
the comics as guideposts while adding their
own spin on things, going more for the "tone

00:02:18.879 --> 00:02:22.180
and feel" of a character than details and
plotlines.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:26.099
And while the movie does feature some nods
to Cable's comic-book backstory, as I've talked

00:02:26.099 --> 00:02:30.329
about in my Deadpool 2 easter eggs video,
the screenwriters made a conscious decision

00:02:30.329 --> 00:02:35.480
not to go heavily into his background as they
felt it was too much information for a 2-hour

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:36.480
film.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:39.730
It's interesting that earlier versions of
the script did include Cable's telekinetic

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:42.930
powers, though in the end they didn't make
it on screen.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:48.030
Of course, Cable will be back in the X-Force
movie and, although they're not writing it,

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:51.629
Deadpool 2's screenwriters say we'll likely
hear more in that film about things like the

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:54.519
techno-organic virus that Cable has in the
comics.

00:02:54.519 --> 00:02:59.549
Also, according to plot leaks, Deadpool 2
originally included a scene of Cable breaking

00:02:59.549 --> 00:03:03.870
into a government facility to steal the time
travel device he uses to go back to find the

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.370
young Firefist.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:09.579
Of course, in the final film, he already has
that device when we first see him in the ruins

00:03:09.579 --> 00:03:10.669
of his former home.

00:03:10.669 --> 00:03:15.120
As I mentioned earlier, it's becoming more
normal for major movies like Deadpool 2 and

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.530
Avengers Infinity War to use fake scenes or
alternate takes in their marketing to avoid

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:20.530
spoilers.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:24.651
In a comedy like Deadpool, tons of stuff was
improvised in addition to the script, with

00:03:24.651 --> 00:03:28.599
Ryan Reynolds delivering multiple riffs on
scenes, which means there were just too many

00:03:28.599 --> 00:03:33.120
jokes to fit in the film, so director David
Leitch deliberately included some of those

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:38.150
alternate versions in marketing materials
while others may appear on the Blu-ray.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:42.480
And to give you a taste of what that included,
here's a stack of alternate and deleted lines

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.560
and moments from the Deadpool 2 trailers which
ended up different in the final film.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.629
"Oh, you're living the dream DP."

00:03:48.629 --> 00:03:49.629
"Yeah."

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:51.849
"Devil may care attitude."

00:03:51.849 --> 00:03:53.139
"Strong thighs."

00:03:53.139 --> 00:03:54.430
"Beautiful girlfriend."

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:56.359
"Sorry I'm late."

00:03:56.359 --> 00:04:00.499
"I was rounding up all the gluten in the world
and launching it into space where it can't

00:04:00.499 --> 00:04:02.180
not hurt us ever again."

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.359
"Move or die!"

00:04:03.359 --> 00:04:05.049
"Pump the hate brakes Thanos!"

00:04:05.049 --> 00:04:07.659
"We're gonna form a super duper f****** group!"

00:04:07.659 --> 00:04:09.830
"It's certainly not very cinematic!"

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:12.300
"You're absolutely right."

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.599
"Now, let's go get our f*** on!"

00:04:15.599 --> 00:04:16.599
"Ooh!

00:04:16.599 --> 00:04:17.599
Yeah!

00:04:17.599 --> 00:04:19.400
Your bullets ... are really fast."

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.400
"Yeah!

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.400
Oh!

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.199
This is what happens when you turn 40."

00:04:24.199 --> 00:04:26.270
"Your time's up you dumb f***!"

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:30.759
"And that is why Sisterhood of the Travelling
Pants is pure pornography."

00:04:30.759 --> 00:04:31.759
"Ahhh."

00:04:31.759 --> 00:04:32.759
"God, I wish I finished college."

00:04:32.759 --> 00:04:37.870
I think some of those trailer lines were funnier
than their counterparts in the movie, though

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:41.780
others in the film were funnier than in the
trailers especially as I wasn't expecting

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:45.000
them, for example, "Pump the hate brakes,
Fox and Friends".

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.009
It's a tricky balance for studios as some
fans might appreciate the pleasant surprise

00:04:49.009 --> 00:04:53.180
of the final movie ending up a bit different,
while others might feel cheated of moments

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.930
they enjoyed in the trailers.

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:59.340
By the way, there was also a joke by Peter
teased in a TV spot that never made it into

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:00.570
the final cut.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.470
"I have both type 1 and 2 diabetes."

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.310
"As it turns out we are looking for someone
with diabetes."

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:07.660
"Peter's your man!"

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:11.879
That line was likely ad-libbed by Rob Delaney
who did a lot of improvisation in his role

00:05:11.879 --> 00:05:12.879
as Peter.

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:16.620
By the way, originally, the filmmakers toyed
with the idea of one of the screenwriters

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:21.840
playing the part of Peter, but Ryan Reynolds
recommended Catastrophe star Delaney.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:26.060
And while we did get some amusing shots of
Wade scooting around the X-Mansion in Professor

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:30.610
X's wheelchair, this one of him spinning around
in front of a couple of portraits of Abraham

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:33.509
Lincoln and Barrack Obama didn't make it into
the movie.

00:05:33.509 --> 00:05:37.560
There's an example of something being digitally
altered between the trailer and the final

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:42.919
film in the propaganda posters behind Firefist
which changed from "The End Is Near" in the

00:05:42.919 --> 00:05:47.289
trailer to "M-Day Is Here" in the movie, which
is a very interesting X-Men easter egg you

00:05:47.289 --> 00:05:50.220
can learn more about in my easter egg video.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:54.629
The Deadpool sequel certainly isn't short
on post-credits scenes as it is; however,

00:05:54.629 --> 00:05:59.350
they also filmed an extra credits scene featuring
baby Hitler which was initially going to appear

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:01.000
at the very end of the movie.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:05.289
The scene was set in a newborn nursery and
showed Deadpool deliberating over whether

00:06:05.289 --> 00:06:07.350
to kill the baby lying in a crib.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:12.659
He eventually decided in favour, saying 'Maximum
effort' as he went in to strangle the infant.

00:06:12.659 --> 00:06:18.479
The scene was deleted after it left test audiences
decidedly uneasy, so it seems infanticide

00:06:18.479 --> 00:06:22.580
was a step too far even for the notoriously
near-the-knuckle comic-book character.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:26.759
According to the screenwriters, there was
also another version drafted of that scene

00:06:26.759 --> 00:06:30.721
which included Deadpool using a pen to draw
a moustache on the baby so he looked more

00:06:30.721 --> 00:06:33.530
like adult Hitler before dispatching him!

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:37.759
By the way, it seems the filmmakers couldn't
entirely resist including a baby Hitler line

00:06:37.759 --> 00:06:39.070
in the film.

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:43.130
Deadpool asks Cable why he didn't just travel
back to when Firefist was a baby and kill

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:47.539
him then, "or better yet, head back a little
further, kill baby Hitler."

00:06:47.539 --> 00:06:51.879
While the baby Hitler end-credits scene was
actually filmed, another idea the writers

00:06:51.879 --> 00:06:54.759
had for the post-credits didn't make it past
the writing stage.

00:06:54.759 --> 00:06:59.710
Basically, it was going to involve more X-Force
interviews, one of them with actor Chris Evans

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:04.180
reprising his role as the Human Torch from
Fox's original Fantastic Four movies.

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:10.280
Sadly, they never got as far as actually asking
Evans, who's now best known as the MCU's Captain

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:11.280
America.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:14.780
However, the reason they didn't end up with
the Human Torch post-credits is that Ryan

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:18.729
Reynolds came up with the idea for the Green
Lantern scene which closes the movie with

00:07:18.729 --> 00:07:22.259
Deadpool travelling back in time to shoot
Reynolds who thinks he's made it to the big

00:07:22.259 --> 00:07:26.039
time after he gets the script for the much-maligned
DC movie.

00:07:26.039 --> 00:07:31.570
Deadpool 2 includes plenty of easter eggs
and jokey references to movies owned by Disney.

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:35.860
However, Ryan Reynolds has said that Fox made
him delete one particular Disney-related joke

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:37.139
from the film.

00:07:37.139 --> 00:07:41.139
Cutting the gag was a "sore spot" for Reynolds,
but while he wouldn't reveal what the joke

00:07:41.139 --> 00:07:45.550
was, he did tell EW that looking back, removing
it was "a wise decision".

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:49.840
Of course, much of Fox has now been bought
by Disney whose CEO has previously said there

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.939
could be room for the R-rated Merc on their
future slate.

00:07:52.939 --> 00:07:57.400
However, the merger deal isn't officially
closed yet and it seems it may have affected

00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:02.879
the virtually-filter-free Deadpool franchise
which normally takes aim at pretty much everything.

00:08:02.879 --> 00:08:06.659
Given the humour in the Deadpool movies, you
can imagine the kind of innuendo the writers

00:08:06.659 --> 00:08:10.300
might have come up with for a joke about Fox
and the Mouse House getting together.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:15.400
But as the "not-safe-for-work" joke was a
bit "too dark" and "at the expense of Disney",

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:18.440
we may never find out exactly what we're missing.

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:22.750
An underwater scene with Deadpool and Vanessa,
who's played by Morena Baccarin, was also

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:24.180
chopped from the movie.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:28.129
The scene in question was a dream sequence
and filming for it involved an apartment set

00:08:28.129 --> 00:08:33.520
being sunk 20 feet under water and Baccarin
being strapped to a chair with weights attached

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:35.410
to her so she stayed in place!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:39.620
Baccarin was actually pretty annoyed it ended
up cut as she had to confront her massive

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:44.710
fear of being underwater both during the shoot
and during the scuba training to prepare for

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:45.710
it.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:49.830
However, as she told GMA, unlike Ryan Reynolds
who seemed completely at ease filming the

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:54.820
scene, she found it hard to relax and thinks
her anxiety may have been picked up on camera,

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:57.200
which could be why the scene was deleted.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:01.390
It sounds like this sequence was how the film
was originally going to depict Vanessa's scenes

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.130
with Deadpool in the afterlife.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:07.710
Instead, in the final film, the afterlife
scenes look like they maybe take some inspiration

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:12.460
from the music video for A-Ha's Take On Me,
which also plays during those scenes.

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:17.160
An alternate early version of the script had
Vanessa leaving Wade and him trying to get

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.160
her back.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:22.320
However, for the screenwriters, Deadpool works
best when he's suffering and has nothing,

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:24.970
so they killed off her character instead.

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:29.470
In the comics, Vanessa is a mutant shape-shifter
known as Copycat and has a much more interesting

00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:33.270
role compared to her part in both Deadpool
movies so far.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:37.630
And considering it's such a self-aware comic-book
movie, the writers' storytelling choice makes

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:40.890
Deadpool 2 less subversive than it likes to
think it is.

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:45.040
Over the years, killing off female characters
merely to motivate male characters and advance

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:49.670
their comic-book stories has been criticised,
with the term "women in refrigerators" or

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:53.360
"fridging" being coined to describe this trope
because women have literally been murdered

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.000
and stuffed in a fridge.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.000
To quote Deadpool.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:57.530
"That's just lazy writing."

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:02.030
And it's especially frustrating that the screenwriters
decided not to develop Vanessa's character

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:05.860
and mutant powers for the sequel as, after
the first movie, they actually said they wanted

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:08.130
to explore that in future films.

00:10:08.130 --> 00:10:12.161
It's also interesting that after the writer's
decided to kill Vanessa off, their original

00:10:12.161 --> 00:10:16.690
plan was for her to stay dead, and that's
exactly what audiences saw happen at the first

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:20.570
screenings of the film, which didn't include
any time-travelling post-credits scenes as

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:22.760
they hadn't come up with the idea at that
point.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.840
The end-credits scenes were actually filmed
during additional photography.

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:30.860
Speaking of extra filming, as is the case
with most major movies, Deadpool 2 did do

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:35.100
some reshoots and, in March this year, there
were reports claiming the movie was suffering

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.060
from poor test screenings.

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:40.740
After the rumours surfaced, counter-reports
appeared in the press, possibly leaked by

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:45.430
the studio, about three separate sets of test
screenings of Deadpool 2, all of which scored

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.220
very highly.

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:51.340
Exactly what went on there isn't totally clear
and the official line is that reshoots were

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:55.530
mostly to add more scenes with the two characters
- Cable and Domino - which test audiences

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:56.530
really liked.

00:10:56.530 --> 00:11:00.860
But I wonder whether the eventual idea to
resurrect Vanessa also came about because

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:03.170
of reactions from those screenings.

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:06.770
Obviously, test screenings are confidential
so there's no way of truly knowing for sure

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:10.330
whether claims about good or bad tests can
be fully trusted.

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:14.870
At end of Deadpool 2, there's a credit that
reads "IN MEMORY OF SEQUANA HARRIS", in honour

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:19.370
of the stuntwoman and pro racer who died in
a motorcycle accident on the set of the movie

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:20.370
in Vancouver.

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:24.161
At the time of the tragic event, Harris was
doubling for Zazie Beetz in what appears to

00:11:24.161 --> 00:11:28.950
have been an action scene of Domino on a motorbike,
and, for obvious reasons, the filmmakers opted

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:32.100
not to reshoot the scene for the final film.

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:36.120
One new character we only saw a little of
in Deadpool 2 was Black Tom Cassidy.

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:40.370
Originally, he was going to have a much bigger
part in the movie, acting as a kind of devil

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:44.460
figure whispering in Russell's ear, pushing
him to criminality.

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:48.470
Comic book fans will know Black Tom as an
X-Men villain and a mutant who can use plant

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:50.470
life to project and manipulate energy.

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:55.200
There are some crazy comic book storylines
with the character and the original idea for

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:58.660
Deadpool 2 was for Black Tom to be the main
villain of the movie.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:02.350
Speaking to CBR, the writers said there was
a scene planned where Black Tom would create

00:12:02.350 --> 00:12:06.580
hailstorms of wood from trees and also move
the entire orphanage.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:11.470
The idea was scrapped though because the cost
of those CG scenes was too high for the budget,

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:15.540
and the filmmakers decided to focus the CG
money instead on Juggernaut.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:20.670
So, that's why ultimately Black Tom Cassidy's
role was cut back and the character was quickly

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.030
killed off.

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:26.220
The writers have said they regret this a little,
but added that they can always use the time

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:28.990
travel device to resurrect him if they want
to.

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:32.980
There's also a joke about a Deadpool 3 movie
which feels like it might have been filmed

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:37.030
specifically for the trailer, but it probably
could also have worked as one of the motormouthed

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:39.180
merc's many meta-moments within the movie.

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:40.860
"It lives up to the hype.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:41.860
Plus, plus."

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:43.610
"F*** it, they probably won't make it three."

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:44.610
"Yeah, why would they?"

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:45.920
"Stop at two.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:47.250
You killed it."

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:51.380
If you're hoping all these deleted scenes
may mean there's a possible extended cut in

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:56.200
the works, then you're likely in luck as director
David Leitch told website Bloody Disgusting

00:12:56.200 --> 00:13:00.160
that he hopes to share some lengthier scenes
when the Blu-ray release comes out.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:04.510
One particular extended scene that Leitch
teased happens in the opening fight montage

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:08.850
and is "a single shot in the bathhouse fight
with the yakuza" which he describes as "a

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:11.160
seamless 360 shot that's really fun".

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:15.560
Something the screenwriters have said will
be on the DVD is a montage of Wade's various

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:18.530
attempts to kill himself after Vanessa's death.

00:13:18.530 --> 00:13:22.330
Because of Deadpool's healing factor, each
attempt fails, of course, but in the extended

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:26.760
scene we see Wade making more and more violent
attempts such as jumping into a polar bear

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:29.890
enclosure and swallowing drain cleaner chemicals.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:34.740
Zazie Beetz also told Digital Spy about a
very funny "back-and-forth" scene between

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:38.310
her and Ryan Reynolds which "everybody loved
[…] – but then parts of the script got

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:40.620
reworked, and so it just didn't fit in anymore."

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:44.780
So, it looks like there's plenty of scope
for bonus Domino and Deadpool deleted scenes

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:45.790
on the Blu-ray!

